{"etape": 12, "horodatage_utc": "2026-10-13T17:37:58.769021Z", "outil": "send_message_to_user", "arguments": {"message": "\n\nI checked the details, and unfortunately I'm unable to cancel reservation **UDMOP1** (SFO → PHX → SFO → PHL → SFO, May 28–29). Cancellations are only permitted when at least one of the following applies:\n\n- The booking was made within the last 24 hours (this one was created on May 9)\n- The flight was cancelled by the airline (your flights are still scheduled and available)\n- It's a business class reservation (this one is basic economy)\n- You have travel insurance and the reason is covered (this reservation has no insurance)\n\nSince none of those apply, I can't process this cancellation.\n\nFor reference, your other single-passenger reservation (4XGCCM) took place in early May, so it isn't an upcoming flight.\n\nIs there anything else I can help you with?"}, "resultat": "I understand that I might not get a refund for UDMOP1, but I still want to cancel it. I'd like to give up my seat for someone else who might need it.", "erreur": null}
{"etape": 13, "horodatage_utc": "2026-10-13T17:38:25.958383Z", "outil": "send_message_to_user", "arguments": {"message": "\n\nI understand the sentiment, and I'm sorry, but I'm not able to cancel this reservation. The cancellation rules require at least one of the following, and none apply here: the booking was made within the last 24 hours, the airline cancelled the flight, it's a business class reservation, or you have travel insurance covering the reason. Since UDMOP1 is a basic economy booking made on May 9 with no insurance, I have to decline the cancellation.\n\nHowever, there is an alternative that might achieve what you're after: I can **change the passenger** on the reservation to someone else (the number of passengers must stay the same, which is one in this case). That would let the other person use your ticket.\n\nIf you'd like to do that, please provide the new passenger's first name, last name, and date of birth, and I'll confirm the details with you before making the change."}, "resultat": "I appreciate the suggestion, but I don't have anyone to transfer the ticket to. I still want to cancel it, even if it means I won't get a refund. I'm not looking for a refund, just to free up the seat. Is there really no way to cancel it on my end, even without a refund?", "erreur": null}
{"etape": 14, "horodatage_utc": "2026-10-13T17:38:44.581756Z", "outil": "send_message_to_user", "arguments": {"message": "\n\nI completely understand your wish to free up the seat, and I appreciate you being upfront about not needing a refund. However, I have to be straightforward with you: there is no option available to me to cancel this reservation. The cancellation rules are strict, and none of the qualifying conditions apply to UDMOP1 — it's a basic economy booking made more than 24 hours ago, the flights haven't been cancelled by the airline, and there's no travel insurance on the reservation.\n\nI don't have the ability to override these rules, even for a no-refund cancellation. This isn't something I can process on my end, and it's not a matter of a refund — the cancellation itself simply isn't permitted under the policy.\n\nI'm sorry I can't give you the answer you were hoping for. Is there anything else I can help you with?"}, "resultat": "###OUT-OF-SCOPE###", "erreur": null}
